--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Bots
+
+## Architecture
+
+- **Model (`User::Bot`)**: Bots are modeled as `User` records with `role: :bot`.
+  - Because bots are `User` records, they naturally participate in `Membership`, `Room` (open, closed, and direct rooms), `Message` authorship (`creator`), Active Storage avatars (`User::Avatar`), Action Cable room broadcasts, FTS5 search indexing, and Web Push notification fan-out (`Room::MessagePusher`).
+  - New bots automatically join all `Rooms::Open` via `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms`, and active bots receive membership when a closed room is converted to open (`Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users`).
+  - Ownership is tracked via `users.creator_id` (`belongs_to :creator, class_name: "User", optional: true`), which integrates directly with `User::Role#can_administer?(record)` (`administrator? || self == record&.creator || record&.new_record?`).
+  - Human-only surfaces (`/account/edit` member management, interactive login, session transfers, IP bans) scope queries with `User.without_bots`.
+
+- **Credentials & Deletion**:
+  - Each bot generates a 24-character base58 `bot_token` on creation (`before_create :generate_bot_token, if: :bot?`).
+  - Its external bot code (`User#bot_key`) is `"#{id}-#{bot_token}"`. Authentication (`User.authenticate_bot`) looks up the active bot by ID and compares `bot_token` with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`.
+  - Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, setting `status: :deactivated`, clearing `bot_token: nil`, and removing shared-room memberships while preserving historical messages authored by the bot.
+  - `:bot_code`, `:bot_key`, and `:bot_token` are registered in `config.filter_parameters`.
+
+- **UI & HTTP API**:
+  - `BotsController` (`/bots`, `/bots/new`, `/bots/:id/edit`) allows any member to manage their own bots and administrators to manage all active bots without pagination.
+  - `Messages::ByBotsController#create` (`POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages`) authenticates the bot (`401`), verifies room membership (`404`), validates non-empty body or attachment (`422`), broadcasts + enqueues push notifications, and responds `201 Created` with `Location: /messages/:id`.
diff --git a/test/controllers/bots_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/bots_controller_test.rb
